  "result": "I fixed it: `Cart.remove` now drops the Widget line.\n\n**Root cause:** in `shop/models.py:33`, `Cart.remove` filtered lines by the item's name (`l.item.name != sku`) instead of its SKU. The demo passes `'sku-1'`, which never matches the name `'Widget'`, so nothing was removed. `Cart.add` already matches on `l.item.sku`, so I changed `remove` to do the same.\n\n**Checks:**\n- `python3 -m shop.demo` now prints `1`, which is just the Gadget line. Before the fix it printed `2`.\n- pytest isn't installed here, so I ran the suite with `python3 -m unittest`: all 6 tests pass.\n- None of the existing tests call `Cart.remove`, so the suite wouldn't have caught this bug. I didn't add a test for it.",
